When a potion cracks when you kick a chest/Box on the ground,
it's effects are spread to a fraction the items inside (maybe 1/2). To
prevent
abuse, all potions that break inside a box/chest is unblessed (but not
uncursed).

So if you break holy water inside a chest, you'll find a lot of rusty
armor/weapons, diluted potions and blanked scrolls :-p

Break cursed water inside a chest, you'll find lots of cursed objects.

So its basically, yet another way to polypile objects (good old
!oPoly), but
only so many will be polyed. Maybe useful for !osickness to poison
many sets of arrows/darts.

This will discourage kicking/using blunt weapons on a box/chest, and
give another advantage to keys/lockpicks.

